  <result aggregation-status="1" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">CSH-I1</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Number of people benefitting fromunconditional and unrestricted cash transfers</narrative>
   </description>
   <indicator aggregation-status="1" ascending="1" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Number of people benefitting fromunconditional and unrestricted cashtransfer</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provide MPCA to ensure beneficiaries&apos; access to diverse and nutritious food, especially for children to 572  households. Each household will be provided with one monthly cash transfers.Provide cash transfer (MPC) that will be sufficient to the returnees households in meeting their monthly basket needs. AWEC will target a 4,004 Total of Beneficiaires (based on a HH Estimation of 7 Members per HH).AWEC will provide MPCA to 572 returnee households. Each household will receive monthly cash assistance aligned with the Minimum Expenditure Basket (MEB) and CashWorking Group guidelines.The intervention includes two key activities:- MPCA transfers to 572 returnee households- 20% MPCA top-up (USD 30) to 150 households with special vulnerabilities, including women-headed households and persons with disabilitiesCash will be distributed through the hawala system using a rolling, batch-wise distribution approach, as returnees arrive continuously. This is not a one-off transfer; distributions will be conducted gradually throughout the project duration. AWEC will conduct regular Post-Distribution Monitoring (PDM) to assess effectiveness, ensure accountability, and inform future improvements.</narrative>
    </description>
