  <result aggregation-status="1" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">HEA-15: Primary health</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Number of primary health careconsultations</narrative>
   </description>
   <indicator aggregation-status="1" ascending="1" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Number of primary health care consultations</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Primary health care, infant and young child feedingsupport will be provided by Integrated Mobile Health and Nutrition Teams (IMHNT). Treatment of common illnesses (e.g., respiratory infections, diarrhoea, malaria); Maternal, newborn, and child health services; Routineimmunization; Family planning and reproductive health; Health education and counselling; Referrals for specialized care when needed will be provided. Further support for  ASH, hygiene promotion,  awareness raising will be done at the facility level.Physical conditions of the 2 facilities will be improved to ensure facility is safe, WASH services available respecting standards and storage conditions for medical supplies areaccording to norms and medical waste is disposed of according to standards.The assumption is that each supported facility will serve 10000 patients monthly for the 6 months. An assumption of 15,000 consultations. Approximation of each individual will have 1.5 consultations within the project period.</narrative>
    </description>
